        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Self-leveling concrete crack filler is the right repair for flat, moving cracks between about 1/8 inch and an inch wide on driveways, patios, sidewalks and garage aprons. It flexes with the slab, levels itself and holds up to traffic when it is installed at the right depth over backer rod.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            It is the wrong repair for walls, hairlines, steep slopes, leaking basement cracks, structural movement and floors you plan to coat. Match the product to the crack, keep it clean and dry, and stop just short of the surface, and a single afternoon of work can keep water out of a slab for years.
          </p>
        </div>

